<p dir="auto">Used before a noun this is a compound modifier and takes a hyphen, matching the leftover pattern of <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5323451413" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45462" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/45462/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45462">#45462</a> and <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5323452038" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45463" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/45463/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45463">#45463</a>. The page slug already uses `object-oriented_programming`.</p>]]></content>
